// Title: User Added To Admin Group Via Dscl
// Sigma ID: b743623c-2776-40e0-87b1-682b975d0ca5
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Sohan G (D4rkCiph3r)
// Date: 2023-03-19 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, initial-access, privilege-escalation, stealth, T1078.003
// Description: Detects attempts to create and add an account to the admin group via "dscl"
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate administration activities
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/master/atomics/T1078.003/T1078.003.md#atomic-test-2---create-local-account-with-admin-privileges---macos
//   - https://ss64.com/osx/dscl.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_dscl_add_user_to_admin_group.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/dscl" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -append " and ProcessCommandLine contains " /Groups/admin " and ProcessCommandLine contains " GroupMembership ")
